            <ArticleTitle>Os vesalianum as a cause of lateral foot pain: a familial case and its treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>56-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a rare case of bilateral symptomatic os vesalianum in a 13-year-old girl whose mother had the same condition unilaterally. We performed osteosynthesis and bone grafting instead of a simple resection to preserve the peroneus brevis tendon, with excellent results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
